==Icelandic==
===Etymology 1===
Old Norse.

====Verb====
'''ríða''' (+ {{dat}})

# to [[ride]] (esp. on [[horseback]])
#: ''[[ekki#Icelandic|Ekki]] '''ríða''' [[hestur#Icelandic|hestinum]] [[minn#Icelandic|mínum]].''
#:: Don't '''ride''' my [[horse]].
# {{vulgar|lang=is}} to [[fuck]], to [[screw]]
#: ''[[langa#Icelandic|Langar]] [[þú#Icelandic|þig]] að '''ríða'''?''
#:: Do you [[want]] to '''fuck'''?
#: '''''Ríddu''' [[ég|mér]].''
#:: '''Fuck''' [[I|me]].

=====Derived terms=====
*[[ríða að fullu]] ("[[exhaust]]")
*[[ríða burtreið]] ("[[tilt]]", "[[joust]]")
*[[reið]]

=====Usage notes=====
* Because the word denotes both the meaning of ''riding an animal'' and ''fucking'', it is often a the subject of [[double entendre]] [[bestiality]] jokes. 

===Etymology 2===
====Verb====
'''ríða''' (+ {{acc}}) ([[reið]], [[riðu]], [[riðið]])
# to [[knot]]
#: ''Að '''ríða''' hnút.''
#:: To '''tie''' a knot.
# to [[braid]] og [[weave]]
#: ''Að '''ríða''' körfu.''
#:: To '''weave''' a basket.
#: ''Að '''ríða''' net.''
#:: To '''weave''' a net.

